# Everything text is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. This machine has core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF checkout breaks two
# things here in ways that are hard to read back from the failure:
#
#   magisk/**/customize.sh, update-binary   Magisk's shell reads a CRLF line as a command with a
#                                           trailing CR. (The Gradle packer normalises these on
#                                           the way into the zip as well - belt and braces,
#                                           because the zip is not the only way they travel.)
#   gradlew                                 a CRLF shebang line is not executable on Linux/macOS,
#                                           so a clone cannot build.
#   scripts/*.sh                            same, for anyone running the device helpers.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git neither diffs nor line-ends them.
*.png            binary
*.webp           binary
*.jar            binary
*.so             binary
*.apk            binary
*.aab            binary
*.dex            binary
*.keystore       binary
*.jks            binary
